**Accumulated Absences Account**

This provision shows the value of the outstanding leave entitlement held by employees of the Authority as at the balance sheet date. Any increase or decrease in the provision is offset by the Accumulated Absences Account (see Note 24a) so that this accounting adjustment does not impact on the level of usable reserves.

**Voluntary Redundancy and Special Payments**

This provision was established in 2010/11 to provide for the additional costs of redundancy and related payments as a result of restructuring within the Authority and potential ill health retirements.

**NNDR Appeals Provision**

This provision shows the Authority’s share of the provision for appeals relating to income from business rates. Due to statutory accounting adjustments, this amount does not impact on the level of the General Fund balance.

**Injury Pension Payments**

This provision has arisen as a result of the requirement to reimburse the Home Office for pension top-up grant claimed in prior years relating to injury awards.

