FROM THE PASTOR by Rev. Dr. Blythe D. Kieffer

They are to do good, to be rich in good works, generous, and ready to share, thus storing up for themselves the treasure of a good foundation for the future, so that they may take hold of the life that really is life.” 1 Timothy 6:18-19

As we begin another year of learning and growing at Westminster, we are grateful for the seasons and rhythm of our life together and for the groundedness within our lives. Stewardship is part of the rhythm of our fall. The 2018 Stewardship Campaign Committee is ably led by Christie Hovey. Serving with Christie are: Cara Barnett, Grady Chronister, Brian Cozadd, Joe Fierstos, Anne Haaker, Dick Herndon, Christy Pound, Sharon Reynolds, Steve Scaife, Betsy Shepherd, and Bill Simpson.

This year’s stewardship theme, Living Generously, based on 1 Timothy 6:18-19, reminds us of the importance of being rich in good works, generous, and ready to share.

The Stewardship letter will be mailed following the Session’s approval of the 2018 budget at the September meeting. The campaign will be introduced the last weekend of September, and the Stewardship Dedication will be the last weekend in October, on Reformation and Harvest Sunday.

MUSIC NOTES by Dale T. Rogers

Mark your calendar for choirs at Westminster.

WESTMINSTER CHOIR begins rehearsal Thursday, September 7 at 7:30 p.m. The annual Choir Retreat will be at Indian Point Presbyterian Church on Saturday, September 9, from 1:30 to 5:00 p.m. Throughout the afternoon, we preview music for the upcoming season through Christmas. The afternoon will close with a service of evensong and a dinner at Los Rancheros in Petersburg.

CHURCH MICE is our music experience for infants to Kindergarteners, based on the early childhood development program, Music Together, from Princeton, New Jersey. Through music, actions, instruments and activity, children learn many life skills and gain knowledge. The program for children and their parents, grandparents or caregivers meets on Saturdays at 11:00 a.m. beginning September 16. You are encouraged to invite friends and neighbors in your play groups to join in the fun. Church Mice is a great way for young families to enter into a fuller church life.

THE WESTMINSTER CHORISTERS (Grades 3-6) will begin Tuesday, September, 12 at 4:45 p.m. following Bridges. Please note the change of rehearsal day from Wednesday to TUESDAY for Choristers.

THE WESTMINSTER CHILDREN’S CHOIR (Kindergarten - Grade 2) will be held on Wednesdays beginning October 11 at 4:45 p.m.

SCOTTISH ORGANIST GORDON STEWART will present an organ concert at Westminster on Friday, October 13 at 7:00 p.m. Gordon is organ tutor for the Organ Scholars at Cambridge University. In this case, Friday the thirteenth is our lucky day!

ADULT EDUCATION

ADULT EDUCATION FORUM FALL SCHEDULE

The Adult Education Forum meets Sunday mornings from 11:15 a.m. to 12 noon in the Second Floor Classroom beginning September 17. The following studies will be presented this fall.

INVITATION TO THE PSALMS
SUNDAYS, SEPTEMBER 17, 24, AND OCTOBER 1

We begin the 2017-2018 Adult Education Forum with the Invitation to the Psalms led by Lyle VanDeventer. Together we will explore the rich diversity of the psalter through DVD presentations and the thoughtful insights presented by the Disciple short-term study.

A MAN NAMED MARTIN
SUNDAYS, OCTOBER 15, 22, 29, NOVEMBER 5, 12, 19, 26, DECEMBER 10 AND 17

On Sunday, October 15 we will begin a DVD series entitled A Man Named Martin in celebration of the 500th Year Anniversary of the Reformation which began when Martin Luther nailed the 95 Thesis on the door of the Castle Church in Wittenberg, Germany on October 31, 1517. The series explores (1) The Man, (2) The Moment, and (3) The Movement in succinct DVD presentations featuring noted theologians. This series will provide bookends to two musical programs featuring music of the Reformation: Scottish Organist Gordon Stewart on Friday, October 13 and the Westminster Christmas Vespers on Sunday, December 10. Join us for these classes as we revisit Church history and the events that shaped who we are today!

PASTOR LED BIBLE STUDIES CONTINUE IN 2017-2018

REV. TRAJAN MCGLL LEADS WEDNESDAY BIBLE STUDY BEGINS SEPTEMBER 13 FROM 7:00 – 8:30 P.M.

Rev. McGill’s Bible Study will move from Tuesday evenings to Wednesday evenings, 7:00–8:30 p.m. beginning September 13. The focus of this year’s study will be good and evil, right and wrong, and justice. Join this discussion of how we live as moral beings in this world and engage in public life from within our identity as Christians.

DR. KIEFFER LEADS THURSDAY BIBLE STUDY BEGINS SEPTEMBER 14 FROM 5:45 – 7:15 P.M.

Dr. Kieffer’s Bible Study will meet on Thursdays, 5:45–7:15 p.m., beginning Thursday, September 14. The year we will study the Prophets and the Letters of Paul in the Disciple III curriculum entitled Remember Who You Are. The Disciple Study books will be available on Commotion Sunday for $30 each. We will revisit Roland H. Bainton’s Christianity at a later time. New members are always welcome to join the journey!

LIBRARIES OPEN ON SUNDAYS THIS FALL

Sunday School and Adult Ed classes have been relocated this fall to provide access to the Rev. Dr. Edward Ziegler Library and the Elaine Ryder Children’s Library.

Special thanks to the Library Committee: Sharon Turner, Chair, Leah Duling, Melanie Green, Ann Hamilton, Pat Hymans and Nancy Scott for their work preparing the libraries for the new program year.

YOUTH UPDATE by Natalie Knox

CONFIRMATION AND JUNIOR HIGH INFO MEETING
COMMOTION SUNDAY, SEPTEMBER 10 AT 9:30 A.M.
Join Natalie Knox for an informational meeting on Commotion Sunday (September 10th) at 9:30 a.m. in the Sanctuary to review the exciting curriculum as our youth learn about the Bible and the Presbyterian Church in preparation for membership.

Youth Group begins Sunday, September 10!

CONFIRMATION AND JUNIOR HIGH YOUTH GROUP
4:00 – 5:30 P.M. (SECOND FLOOR)
Confirmation is the process through which our young people affirm the vows made at their Baptism and become active members of the Presbyterian Church (U.S.A.). At WPC, this journey is woven into fellowship time to build relationships.

CONFIRMATION PREP (GRADES 6-7) provides a solid grounding in the Bible, allowing for more expanded areas of study in 8th grade and high school. This year, 6th and 7th graders will study the Old Testament through the curriculum Echo the Story, which offers creative responses and imaginative engagement with the biblical narratives. Teachers: Sally Godbey, Jim Kincaid, Anna Koeppel & Sarah Zerfas

CONFIRMATION (GRADE 8) focuses on Christian history, Presbyterian theology and polity, and other religious traditions as the young people explore their individual lives of faith. Over the course of the year, students will visit other worshiping communities, build relationships with adult mentors, serve the community and write their own statements of faith. Teachers: Natalie Knox, Marc DeJong with guests including the pastors.

Following class, all three grades come together for fellowship, fun and games in the Youth Room.

YOUTH DINNER 5:30 – 6:00 P.M. (PARISH HALL)
Grades 6-12 gather for fellowship and dinner prepared by parents. A link is available on the WPC website (under Youth Ministries) to sign up and will be emailed out prior to Commotion Sunday.

SR. HIGH YOUTH GROUP 6:00 –7:30 P.M. (YOUTH ROOM)
Youth in grades 9-12 gather weekly to navigate their faith journey, participate in Bible study, worship together, and build relationships. Our theme this year is Messy Stories from the Old Testament. We will examine, discover and reflect on ways we are called to serve the world and how our faith is lived. Along with opportunities for community service throughout the year, our youth participate in an annual Mission Trip and host fundraisers to support their work. Leaders: Natalie Knox, Susan Day, Bill Deemer and Jen DeJong

SATURDAY EVENING SENIOR HIGH BIBLE STUDY continues this month with a dinner at the DeJong home (1955 Illini Rd) on Saturday, September 23rd at 5:00 pm, with Bible study to follow. As always, friends are welcomed and encouraged!

WPC YOUNG ADULTS MEET SUNDAY, SEPTEMBER 24
Young Adults (ages 18-29) will gather on the last Sunday of each month for brunch following worship. This semester’s dates are: September 24, October 29, and November 26th. In September, we will meet at Obed and Isaac’s at 11:30 a.m!

CHILDREN MINISTRIES by Rev. Sarah Iliff McGill

FALL SUNDAY SCHOOL BEGINS SEPTEMBER 10
REGISTRATION AND TEACHER COMMISSIONING
Parents are asked to register their children for Fall Sunday School on or before Commotion Sunday, September 10. The following classes begin and the leaders listed will be commissioned on September 10:

Pre-K–Grade 1 (Third Floor Chapel): Young Children and Worship is a spiritual formation approach which invites children to experience the wonder of God through a storytelling format and multi-sensory materials. Leaders: Rev. Sarah Iliff McGill, Cara Barnett, Cathy Brower, Matthew Knox, Valerie Leonatti, Leigh Milward, Emma Shafer, Karen Sherrick.

Grade 2–3 (Third Floor Classroom): Whirly Spark House is a lectionary-centered curriculum. Children will dive into the Bible together and learn Bible basics that will prepare them to receive their own NRSV Bible as a gift from the congregation at the end of their third grade year. Teachers: Meridith Bryans, Sue Cull, Marc DeJong, and Sara Eldridge.

Grade 4–5 (Third Floor Tower Room): Whirly Spark House is a lectionary-centered curriculum that includes animated videos to set up the lesson, and then dives deeper into the Bible. Teachers: Jen DeJong, Tom Klein, Priscilla Kluge, Lisa Metzger, Angie Musick, and Mary Ray.

WHITNEY BECK SPEARIE RETIRES AS NURSERY WORKER
We are grateful to Whitney Beck Spearie who has worked in our nursery since March 2016. We are happy to announce Whitney is expecting a child this February! Anyone interested in serving our youngest members please contact Rev. Sarah.

BRIDGES MID-WEEK FELLOWSHIP
MOVES TO TUESDAYS BEGINNING SEPTEMBER 12
Children in Grades 3-5 are invited to Bridges on Tuesdays beginning September 12, from 4:00 – 4:45 p.m. This fellowship bridges friendships among our children and across generations. It also includes mission projects. The 2017-2018 theme is “Being a Thoughtful Christian.” This after-school program precedes Westminster Choristers which meets from 4:45 – 5:30 p.m. Leaders: Dr. Kieffer, Rev. Sarah Iliff McGill, and Brad Steller

PARENT FELLOWSHIP GROUP MEETS OCTOBER 7
Parents are invited to gather once a month for camaraderie on the first Saturday of every month. Please join us at the McGill home on October 7 at 5:30 (218 Twin Oaks, Rochester).

CHILDREN OF ABRAHAM
WPC HOSTS WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 4, 4:30 – 6 P.M.
