NEW PROJECT PROPOSALS WELCOME

The Mission and Community Service Committees have this year been ramping up our church’s mission giving, thanks to your extra giving to the endowment—but also thanks to your ideas! We have enjoyed hearing from many of our members recently and supporting the kinds of mission and service in which they are involved. If you have ideas for growing our church’s mission in the world, the committees would love to hear them. For more info on submitting your own proposals, speak to the committee chairpersons, Kay Smith and Peter Kieffer, or to Trajan McGill.

HURRICANE RELIEF DONATIONS

Our denominational disaster relief agency, Presbyterian Disaster Assistance, already has an advance team on the ground in the wake of Hurricane Harvey, surveying the needs and making preparations for a long-term stay in the region. They would love to have our help! Monetary gifts to Westminster marked “Hurricane Relief” will be quickly passed along to support this effort. Thanks also to Brad Milliman, who coordinated a quick response in the first days after the storm, gathering some immediate, emergency supplies to transport himself to Texas.

GIVE-A-MEAL-A-MONTH SEPTEMBER MENU:

Spaghetti Sauce, Pasta, canned or bottled 100% juice, and 100% juice or water canned fruit. Thank you to those who place items in the West Narthex baskets for the Central Illinois Foodbank. Items in High Demand: feminine hygiene products, shampoo, diapers & wipes, granola / nutri-grain / breakfast bars, individual cereal packs, soap.

HELPING HANDS

