VOLUNTEERS ARE NEEDED!

Join the many members of Westminster who have joined together to serve at-risk children attending Graham Elementary School. Central Baptist Church partners with us in providing this after-school program from 3:00 – 6:00 p.m. on Tuesdays. Consider becoming part of the team! For information or questions, call Ann Collins at 622-3847. Sign up on Commotion Sunday.

CHURCH WORLD SERVICE CROP WALK

WORLD COMMUNION SUNDAY, OCTOBER 1

1:00 P.M. AT THIRD PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH

Join the Springfield community as we address hunger in our world and community. The walk begins at Third Presbyterian Church (1030 North Seventh St). Check-in is at 1:00 p.m. with the walk start time of 1:30 p.m.

The final total for the Springfield 2016 Walk was $12,499. Of that amount, 25% goes to our local food pantries. The remainder is used by CWS to fight hunger throughout the world. Food pantries receiving funds include First Presbyterian Food Pantry, Grace Lutheran Food Pantry, Kumler Outreach Ministries and Pleasant Plains Food Pantry.

Members are invited to support Westminster youth walking this year or join them on this meaningful and symbolic journey. Krista Steller is one of the event coordinators and Becky Martin is organizing the Westminster walkers. Donations can be made online at: https://www.crophungerwalk.org/springfield/Team/View/46651/Westminster-Pres or to Westminster by check with a note on the memo to CROP Walk.

